y  did not fall  and would continue to flourish for  another 1 000 years  although they viewed themselves as  simply the romans later historians have  labeled this empire the byzantine empire  after the original name of the old greek  colony byzantium located at the site  where constantinople would later be  built  today the same city has undergone yet  one more name change and is now istanbul  in turkey  the city of constantinople founded in  330 at the site of the old greek city of  byzantium by the roman emperor  constantine the first increased in power  and opulence under his successes until  it rivaled rome itself and surpassed all  other cities of the eastern  mediterranean  the city's status was further enhanced  by the decision of the orthodox  ecumenical council of constantinople to  make that city's bishop the patriarch  second in precedence only to the pope in  rome  of the approximately  95 emperors who ruled over  constantinople  the most significant of the earlier ones  was a man named justinian  his rise to power began as a boy when  his uncle justin became emperor and took  on his nephew as an assistant  justinian quickly became his uncle's  main confidant and advisor  and when his uncle became senile took  over de facto administration of the  empire  upon his uncle's death in 527  justinian succeeded him and embarked on  an energetic program of building  organization and conquest  spectacular rebuilding of the city's  defenses and of the great church of  hagia sophia further enhanced  constantinople status as the greatest  city of western afro-eurasia  the city lost some of its splendor in  the 7th and 8th centuries following a  series of natural disasters and  desperate sieges but in the 9th century  a military and economic recovery took  place leading to the great cultural  achievements of the middle byzantine  period and the city's reputation as a  place protected by military and  commercial strength and by god  an unbroken succession of roman emperors  ruled over this eastern or byzantine  empire  all the way up until 1453  when constantinople at last fell to the  ottoman turks  it might seem odd to us today to speak  of a roman empire  that does not include rome or italy  but the byzantines certainly regarded  themselves as real romans and pretty  much everyone at the time thought so as  well  if one accepts the eastern empire and  its rulers as being romans  a legitimate argument can therefore be  made that the roman empire did not fall  until 1453  and indeed this is the date that is  favored by many historians  [Music]  hey thanks for watching if you'd like to  learn more about the topics in this  episode the full list of series that  these clips came from is in the  description below you can watch them all  on one dream and don't forget to  subscribe to this youtube channel for  new episodes of perspectives and you can  watch previous ones here

